WEBVTT

00:00.790 --> 00:04.230
This is such a nice shop, Eno!

00:04.230 --> 00:08.030
It's a huge change from when you 
were holed up in that cave!

00:08.030 --> 00:10.110
All your hard work paid off, huh?

00:10.110 --> 00:12.230
All thanks to you, Azusa!

00:12.230 --> 00:17.930
If I didn't have a mentor like you, 
I'm certain I'd still be brooding in that cave.

00:17.930 --> 00:22.110
But now even my personality is much 
brighter and more assertive!

00:22.480 --> 00:25.340
I can't even begin to express 
my respect for you!

00:25.340 --> 00:26.680
Oh, yeah?

00:27.060 --> 00:29.370
This bottle is great!

00:29.370 --> 00:33.870
The size is perfect for 
someone living alone!

00:34.280 --> 00:38.380
Hey, Halkara! 
Don't steal other people's ideas!

00:38.380 --> 00:40.200
I wouldn't do that!

00:40.200 --> 00:41.850
I'll just use it as a reference.

00:41.850 --> 00:43.970
That's literally what we 
call "stealing my idea"!

00:43.970 --> 00:46.790
Okay, okay, stop!

00:46.790 --> 00:49.490
I can't tell you to play nice since 
you're business rivals,

00:49.490 --> 00:50.600
but don't fight.

00:52.800 --> 00:56.840
Oh, right. About the mandragora 
pills you wanted...

00:56.840 --> 00:58.620
I have just the thing.

00:59.150 --> 01:02.360
Ta-da! Fully mature mandragora pills!

01:02.710 --> 01:05.200
Fully mature mandragora pills?

01:05.200 --> 01:10.380
Yes. They're normally made with 
three-year-old mandragoras,

01:10.380 --> 01:12.880
but these are made with 
ten-year-old mandragoras!

01:12.880 --> 01:15.890
It's a rare product that can 
only be made in small quantities!

01:15.890 --> 01:19.120
And you're okay with giving it to me?

01:19.120 --> 01:20.840
Please, it's all yours!

01:21.160 --> 01:24.290
I'll make something even 
more amazing someday!

01:24.290 --> 01:27.010
Like super-high-quality, even more mature

01:27.010 --> 01:30.730
mandragora pills made from 
300-year-old mandragoras!

01:30.730 --> 01:32.740
Three hundred years old?!

01:32.740 --> 01:36.240
Yes! They're the rarest of the rare!

01:36.240 --> 01:42.750
To make medicine from 300-year-old 
mandragoras is every witch's dream!

01:43.540 --> 01:44.730
Is that so?

01:44.730 --> 01:49.820
Apparently, mandragoras evolve in some 
crazy way when they've lived 300 years!

01:49.820 --> 01:51.510
They can move around on their own

01:51.510 --> 01:53.870
and even speak in human language!

01:54.290 --> 01:57.060
Isn't it a totally different 
lifeform at that point?

01:57.060 --> 01:58.880
That can't really be...

02:14.570 --> 02:25.580
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

03:36.150 --> 03:40.780
<b>We Went Looking for a Mandragora</b>

03:36.440 --> 03:38.450
Are you serious?!

03:38.450 --> 03:41.230
Where?! Where did you see it?!

03:41.230 --> 03:44.120
Okay, just calm down, Eno.

03:44.120 --> 03:46.680
It might have been some kind of mistake.

03:46.680 --> 03:49.910
And if we're going to go look 
there, we need permission.

03:49.910 --> 03:52.120
The land is privately owned.

03:52.120 --> 03:55.960
Oh, I know what you're talking about! 
Beelzebub's garden, right?

03:56.420 --> 03:59.720
Beelzebub? 
The demon Minister of Agriculture?!

04:00.180 --> 04:03.410
That wasn't so much a garden 
as an entire forest.

04:03.410 --> 04:05.210
Nothing we find there would surprise me.

04:08.120 --> 04:11.310
The shop's closed for the day! 
Please leave now!

04:11.730 --> 04:13.580
Faster, wyvern!

04:14.890 --> 04:17.660
Oh, boy. She's already gone.

04:17.660 --> 04:22.090
Is a 300-year-old mandragora that exciting?

04:22.470 --> 04:26.480
I'm sure there are many witches 
who'd love to have one.

04:26.480 --> 04:29.130
Personally, I'd keep my 
distance from it, but...

04:29.130 --> 04:30.540
Really? Why?

04:30.840 --> 04:34.600
Well, it's a creature that 
talks and moves around.

04:34.600 --> 04:38.790
An elf could never turn something 
like that into medicine.

04:39.940 --> 04:43.540
Wait, making medicine from it just means

04:43.540 --> 04:47.000
borrowing a few of its leaves 
or something, right?

04:47.390 --> 04:50.370
I believe you'd have to 
crush up the entire thing.

04:53.650 --> 04:55.890
Wake up, Flatorte!

04:55.890 --> 04:58.550
I need you to fly right now!

05:00.440 --> 05:04.230
So you took off after her 
in a hurry, but lost her?

05:04.230 --> 05:07.370
You probably just passed her somewhere.

05:08.300 --> 05:09.740
How careless of us.

05:10.130 --> 05:12.700
In any case, I understand the situation.

05:12.700 --> 05:15.340
If I see any strange 
witches on the grounds,

05:15.340 --> 05:17.580
I shouldn't do anything to them, right?

05:17.580 --> 05:22.090
Also, I'd like you to protect 
that mandragora if you can.

05:22.090 --> 05:25.760
Protect a walking plant from that garden?

05:26.150 --> 05:28.490
That sounds like a real hassle.

05:28.970 --> 05:32.470
Beelzebub!

05:32.790 --> 05:34.500
Please open up!

05:33.170 --> 05:36.470
Wh-What is going on here?!

05:34.500 --> 05:36.470
Hello!

05:36.470 --> 05:37.840
Hello in there!

05:37.840 --> 05:39.410
Good day to you!

05:39.980 --> 05:43.240
I apologize for dropping by unannounced!

05:43.240 --> 05:47.330
I heard there was a 300-year-old 
mandragora here

05:47.330 --> 05:48.870
and couldn't just sit around!

05:49.250 --> 05:52.620
I've come to get my hands on it, 
even if it means breaking some laws!

05:52.620 --> 05:55.490
<i>She just declared her intent 
to commit a crime!</i>

05:55.790 --> 05:59.330
Go away! Why are there so 
many of you, anyway?!

05:59.330 --> 06:02.560
To make sure we find the mandragora!

06:02.560 --> 06:05.340
I gathered witches from all over the land

06:05.340 --> 06:08.090
with an agreement to share the 
mandragora once we find it!

06:08.090 --> 06:10.930
This is any witch's greatest wish!

06:10.930 --> 06:13.470
It's the most promising lead I've 
found in a century of searching!

06:13.470 --> 06:16.050
They want it that badly?

06:16.050 --> 06:18.190
Their enthusiasm is incredible...

06:18.450 --> 06:21.510
Strike while the iron's hot! 
Begin the operation!

06:25.030 --> 06:27.350
Hey! Hold it!

06:27.350 --> 06:28.780
Stop this, Eno!

06:29.740 --> 06:31.140
I'm sorry, Azusa!

06:31.140 --> 06:34.120
It must be done if we're to make 
the best medicine in the world!

06:34.120 --> 06:34.620
Bye!

06:34.620 --> 06:37.950
You said you couldn't begin to 
express your respect for me!

06:40.970 --> 06:42.740
Okay, I've had it!

06:42.740 --> 06:45.280
I'll burn the whole garden to ashes!

06:45.280 --> 06:48.380
Don't do that! 
You'll burn the mandragora, too!

06:58.900 --> 07:03.280
We'll just have to find the mandragora 
before Eno and her group does!

07:03.280 --> 07:05.180
We won't let them win!

07:05.410 --> 07:09.490
Be careful. We don't know what 
might live in this garden.

07:09.490 --> 07:10.570
And Halkara—

07:10.850 --> 07:13.330
You're caught already!

07:13.610 --> 07:14.440
Huh?

07:14.440 --> 07:16.320
Oh, no! When did this happen?!

07:20.280 --> 07:22.420
Hey! My clothes!

07:22.420 --> 07:24.750
Wow, her clothes are melting.

07:28.320 --> 07:29.130
Ow!

07:30.430 --> 07:32.850
Thank you so much.

07:32.850 --> 07:36.420
I thought your knowledge of 
forests might help us here.

07:36.420 --> 07:39.030
Maybe I should've had you stay behind.

07:43.440 --> 07:44.810
Master...

07:45.780 --> 07:49.590
There's no sign of the 
mandragora passing this way.

07:49.590 --> 07:53.790
This moss doesn't look like 
it's been stepped on at all.

07:55.120 --> 07:58.990
And this tree is a type that 
grows very thick roots,

07:58.990 --> 08:02.290
so it would be difficult for 
anything to move underground.

08:03.010 --> 08:04.450
Which means...

08:04.450 --> 08:07.080
If we rule out the areas 
near this type of tree,

08:07.080 --> 08:08.910
we can figure out where it is!

08:09.280 --> 08:12.920
Thanks, Halkara! 
You're really on fire today!

08:13.330 --> 08:15.810
No, really, it was nothing...

08:15.810 --> 08:17.790
You're caught again!

08:18.060 --> 08:19.940
Eek! When did that happen?!

08:19.940 --> 08:22.060
You might as well just strip naked!

08:22.060 --> 08:24.720
You know she can't do that!

08:26.380 --> 08:30.050
I knew following her would be a good idea!

08:34.360 --> 08:36.470
Does this area seem suspicious?

08:36.470 --> 08:39.910
Yes. My elven senses are screaming.

08:39.910 --> 08:41.370
There's no doubt about it.

08:42.450 --> 08:44.240
Is that so?

08:46.590 --> 08:47.820
Eno!

08:48.490 --> 08:50.680
You followed us?!

08:50.680 --> 08:53.810
Who was it that told me not 
to steal people's ideas?

08:53.810 --> 08:54.880
That's playing dirty!

08:54.880 --> 08:59.380
A 300-year-old mandragora 
is every witch's dream.

08:59.380 --> 09:01.400
I'll do whatever it takes.

09:04.220 --> 09:06.400
Doesn't the same go for you?

09:06.400 --> 09:08.400
You want to get that mandragora

09:08.400 --> 09:12.350
for maximum honor and glory 
as a witch, do you not?

09:14.090 --> 09:18.730
A mandragora that can walk and 
talk isn't just a plant anymore!

09:19.110 --> 09:21.250
It's the same as us!

09:21.250 --> 09:25.750
I can't sit around and let 
a life like that be taken!

09:27.500 --> 09:30.730
It seems neither of us is willing to yield.

09:30.730 --> 09:34.880
But no matter what you say, 
I'm getting that mandragora!

09:45.780 --> 09:48.630
This is bad! There are too many of them!

09:48.630 --> 09:50.780
They're going to find it before we do!

09:50.780 --> 09:53.140
The moment of destiny is at hand!

09:53.140 --> 09:55.180
Everyone, fight!

09:56.060 --> 09:58.130
We have to find it quick!

09:58.130 --> 10:01.350
Hey! Get out here, mandragora!

10:01.350 --> 10:03.850
As if it's gonna show up if you do that!

10:03.850 --> 10:07.740
Wait... You're sure this 
mandragora spoke, right?

10:08.070 --> 10:12.450
And it ran away when it realized 
you were a witch, right?

10:12.450 --> 10:13.270
Yeah.

10:14.010 --> 10:15.290
In that case...

10:16.520 --> 10:20.250
Mandragora! You're in trouble!

10:20.250 --> 10:23.340
You're about to get caught 
and turned into medicine!

10:23.340 --> 10:26.670
The only way to survive is to let 
this Witch of the Highlands here,

10:26.670 --> 10:29.780
Lady Azusa, assume custody of you!

10:29.780 --> 10:34.010
Now, come and leap into Lady Azusa's bosom!

10:37.610 --> 10:38.650
Found it!

10:38.030 --> 10:38.830
Wait!

10:38.330 --> 10:39.360
It's fast!

10:39.360 --> 10:40.610
Whoa!

10:42.530 --> 10:44.910
H-Help me!

10:52.710 --> 10:55.430
I'm taking this girl into my care!

10:55.430 --> 10:58.930
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

10:59.260 --> 11:01.690
I'm taking this girl into my care!

11:01.690 --> 11:04.340
If anyone has a problem 
with that, bring it on!

11:06.700 --> 11:09.200
Azusa, are you sure about this?

11:09.200 --> 11:13.970
That's a genuine 300-year-old mandragora.

11:15.460 --> 11:16.920
Sorry about this.

11:17.440 --> 11:19.480
Hey! What are you doing?!

11:19.740 --> 11:21.620
Let me ask <i>you</i> something, Eno.

11:21.620 --> 11:25.230
Can you crush up an innocent little girl 
like this and make her into medicine?

11:27.740 --> 11:29.620
When you put it that way...

11:31.410 --> 11:35.400
I was imagining something 
with a more monstrous form.

11:35.400 --> 11:38.060
I never thought it'd be a 
cute little girl like this.

11:38.420 --> 11:39.370
Right?

11:39.370 --> 11:40.930
Yeah, she's cute.

11:40.930 --> 11:42.700
She actually is.

11:41.650 --> 11:44.400
No matter how long I've dreamed of this...

11:44.400 --> 11:46.720
I can't make her into medicine.

11:47.930 --> 11:51.770
Well, either way, you're the 
one who caught her first.

11:51.770 --> 11:54.660
We have no right to do anything.

11:54.660 --> 11:58.100
Then let's call this matter settled.

11:58.100 --> 11:59.150
Hang on.

12:01.390 --> 12:02.360
Here.

12:02.360 --> 12:05.310
What?! I can have that?!

12:05.310 --> 12:08.180
My roots are my body, 
so I can't give you that,

12:08.180 --> 12:10.450
but I can always regrow my leaves.

12:12.030 --> 12:16.260
But in return, you have to promise 
you won't come after me!

12:16.670 --> 12:18.140
Understood!

12:18.140 --> 12:22.460
Eno, Witch of the Cave, 
will never come after you again!

12:22.750 --> 12:25.970
I guess the matter really is settled now.

12:27.080 --> 12:29.720
So this is the leaf of a 
300-year-old mandragora!

12:29.720 --> 12:31.220
The real deal!

12:31.650 --> 12:32.970
Hold it.

12:33.330 --> 12:35.490
I'm giving you this.

12:36.640 --> 12:37.900
What is it?

12:38.390 --> 12:40.800
An invoice for reparations

12:40.800 --> 12:44.370
for trespassing on private property 
and ransacking my garden.

12:44.370 --> 12:47.870
If you fail to pay, 
I will have to take other measures.

12:49.900 --> 12:53.360
I'm the one who's been put 
through the most trouble here.

12:53.360 --> 12:55.550
She's so calculating.

12:55.550 --> 12:59.610
Anyway, I think the matter 
really <i>is</i> settled now.

13:00.980 --> 13:03.890
Halkara was the real MVP this time!

13:04.420 --> 13:08.770
If you hadn't done what you did, 
Eno's group might've caught this kid.

13:10.200 --> 13:14.570
Well, when it comes to plants, 
you can always count on an elf!

13:14.570 --> 13:15.320
I hate them.

13:15.320 --> 13:16.150
Wha?

13:16.410 --> 13:18.470
I hate elves.

13:18.470 --> 13:19.400
Huh?!

13:19.400 --> 13:22.020
'Cause they pick plants.

13:22.020 --> 13:27.650
W-Well, yes, but I wouldn't 
hurt a living being like you!

13:27.650 --> 13:29.880
Just the fact that you're an elf scares me.

13:29.880 --> 13:31.660
Don't come near me.

13:31.660 --> 13:34.030
Grr... Rawr!

13:34.310 --> 13:35.780
Eek!

13:35.780 --> 13:38.060
So they're your natural enemy, huh?

13:38.060 --> 13:40.360
I guess you really are a plant.

13:40.360 --> 13:45.050
I am! I lived a long time, 
and before I knew it, I looked like this.

13:45.510 --> 13:48.050
So what are you going to do now?

13:48.510 --> 13:52.050
I wouldn't mind if you were 
to return to the garden.

13:54.350 --> 13:57.050
Well, it's not that much fun here.

14:01.270 --> 14:03.770
There's not much sunlight,

14:03.770 --> 14:06.310
and it's nutritionally deficient.

14:06.590 --> 14:11.700
So if there's a safer place to live, 
I wouldn't mind moving.

14:11.910 --> 14:13.710
Want to live with me, then?

14:15.250 --> 14:19.060
I have a field in my yard, 
so you won't need to hold back.

14:19.500 --> 14:23.370
And it's a good environment 
for plants to grow?

14:23.370 --> 14:27.140
I don't think any witches would 
come around looking for you.

14:27.140 --> 14:31.220
And it's in the highlands, 
so you'd get lots of sunlight.

14:31.610 --> 14:34.740
Th-Then I guess I'll give it a try.

14:34.740 --> 14:36.720
Take me with you.

14:36.720 --> 14:40.050
Yay! Our family's growing!

14:40.050 --> 14:41.620
Who are you calling "family"?!

14:41.620 --> 14:43.400
Don't throw me together with an elf!

14:43.400 --> 14:46.990
Rawr!

14:45.450 --> 14:46.990
I'm sorry!

14:46.990 --> 14:49.220
Well, see you later, Beelzebub.

14:49.220 --> 14:51.250
Sorry for all the trouble.

14:51.250 --> 14:52.110
Indeed.

14:52.470 --> 14:56.130
And be well, um...

14:56.670 --> 14:59.590
Come to think of it, 
I don't know your name.

14:59.590 --> 15:03.340
I don't have one. I never needed a name.

15:03.340 --> 15:06.440
Then the great Flatorte will name you!

15:06.440 --> 15:07.840
Since you're a mandragora...

15:08.080 --> 15:09.210
"Drago."

15:11.090 --> 15:14.450
Don't give me a name that 
sounds like a dragon's name!

15:14.450 --> 15:15.870
Are you dumb?!

15:15.870 --> 15:16.970
Excuse me?!

15:16.970 --> 15:21.090
Well... how about 
"Giant Running Mandragora"?

15:21.090 --> 15:23.190
You be quiet, elf!

15:23.190 --> 15:24.110
Rawr!

15:24.780 --> 15:26.850
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

15:26.850 --> 15:30.050
Can't you use something 
simple like "Grass 1"?

15:30.050 --> 15:32.620
Out of the question! Rawr! Rawr!

15:32.620 --> 15:35.890
We need some kind of starting point.

15:35.890 --> 15:37.770
Is there anything you like?

15:37.770 --> 15:39.680
Dirt, water, and sand!

15:39.680 --> 15:42.170
Dirt, water, and sand, huh?

15:44.500 --> 15:48.850
<i>Sand... Well, that's 
pretty straightforward.</i>

15:48.850 --> 15:51.060
<i>Sand... Sand...</i>

15:51.520 --> 15:52.780
<i>Sandra?</i>

15:53.640 --> 15:56.640
Sandra! Your name is Sandra!

15:57.120 --> 15:58.230
Sandra?

15:58.520 --> 16:00.740
Oh, that's very cute!

16:00.740 --> 16:02.490
It has a nice ring to it!

16:02.490 --> 16:03.930
Sandra...

16:03.930 --> 16:07.810
W-Well, I suppose I have no 
choice but to live with it.

16:12.940 --> 16:14.370
Hey, Sandra.

16:14.370 --> 16:15.500
What?

16:15.500 --> 16:19.550
There's something I'd like you to promise me 
before we reach my house in the highlands.

16:19.550 --> 16:20.830
What's that?

16:21.080 --> 16:23.310
Get along with my family.

16:23.310 --> 16:27.340
You can argue every now and then, 
but you must always make up.

16:28.880 --> 16:31.590
Fine. I'll try my best.

16:40.390 --> 16:42.180
Yay!

16:42.880 --> 16:45.760
Nice to meet you! I'm Falfa!

16:45.760 --> 16:48.440
I'm her younger sister, Shalsha. Welcome.

16:49.050 --> 16:50.690
Go on, Sandra.

16:51.230 --> 16:52.870
Nice to meet you.

16:53.430 --> 16:57.280
Looks like she's just a bit 
younger than these two.

16:57.680 --> 16:59.450
I'm a big sister!

16:59.700 --> 17:03.450
<i>Sandra is actually a whole 
lot older, though...</i>

17:04.110 --> 17:07.470
Everyone, dinner is ready!

17:07.800 --> 17:10.090
Come eat with us, Sandra.

17:10.090 --> 17:11.390
I don't need to.

17:11.390 --> 17:12.470
Huh?!

17:19.290 --> 17:21.740
The only food I need is water.

17:21.740 --> 17:24.730
Then I just need sunlight 
to photosynthesize.

17:24.730 --> 17:26.430
That makes sense...

17:26.430 --> 17:28.880
Which room would you like?

17:28.880 --> 17:31.570
You can share Falfa and 
Shalsha's if you want.

17:31.570 --> 17:33.630
Your vegetable garden will be fine.

17:33.630 --> 17:36.810
I'm more comfortable on dirt. 
I'll sleep there, too.

17:36.810 --> 17:40.090
Well, she's definitely a plant.

17:40.390 --> 17:42.640
Thanks for dinner!

17:43.310 --> 17:46.150
You both left your vegetables 
untouched again.

17:46.150 --> 17:48.170
I'm already full.

17:48.170 --> 17:49.210
Me, too.

17:49.210 --> 17:51.960
No, you need to eat your vegetables.

17:51.960 --> 17:54.420
You can't blame them. They're yucky.

17:58.400 --> 17:59.570
Sandra...

18:01.930 --> 18:03.830
What... d-did you just...

18:04.620 --> 18:06.850
The vegetables here are yucky.

18:08.600 --> 18:10.040
C-Come on!

18:10.040 --> 18:13.080
How can you tell when you 
haven't even eaten them?!

18:13.080 --> 18:16.240
When you've been a plant as 
long as I have, you can tell.

18:16.480 --> 18:19.700
They're not... that bad, are they?

18:19.700 --> 18:21.970
No, I don't think so!

18:21.970 --> 18:24.750
I can enjoy anything I eat!

18:24.750 --> 18:28.250
I've never eaten them, so I can't say.

18:28.250 --> 18:30.990
You guys aren't helping at all...

18:31.250 --> 18:33.400
Don't get all sad about it just yet.

18:33.400 --> 18:36.210
If you really want to make 
these two eat vegetables,

18:36.210 --> 18:38.020
I have an idea.

18:38.020 --> 18:39.260
Really?!

18:39.580 --> 18:43.500
Cabbage and carrots should be just 
about ready to harvest now.

18:43.500 --> 18:45.650
I'll help you.

18:45.650 --> 18:46.990
Then...

18:47.250 --> 18:51.400
the quality of the food you 
eat here will go up a level.

18:55.500 --> 18:58.750
The most basic need for 
plants is always dirt.

18:58.750 --> 19:03.730
They like soft, fluffy soil that's 
full of air and has good drainage.

19:05.040 --> 19:09.810
Then till that soil with compost 
that's full of organic matter.

19:09.810 --> 19:12.490
And don't forget to spread some lime.

19:12.490 --> 19:13.760
Lime?

19:13.760 --> 19:15.870
Please explain why.

19:15.870 --> 19:19.560
To make the soil slightly acidic, 
making it easier for veggies to grow.

19:19.920 --> 19:23.800
From there, you just need me to 
bring plenty of nutrients to them.

19:23.800 --> 19:26.700
How are you doing that, exactly?

19:26.700 --> 19:28.280
That's a secret.

19:29.590 --> 19:32.170
And now it's finally time to harvest.

19:32.170 --> 19:35.690
Just look at how these veggies shine! 
Don't they look happy?

19:35.690 --> 19:38.880
Anyway, that's what you get 
when you have my help.

19:40.970 --> 19:43.190
It's done!

19:43.560 --> 19:46.460
Fried carrots, carrot potage,

19:46.460 --> 19:49.450
and stir-fried cabbage and carrots!

19:49.450 --> 19:51.460
They all look delicious!

19:53.890 --> 19:56.560
There's no meat in any of it.

19:56.560 --> 19:58.470
This is food for adults.

19:58.470 --> 20:01.550
I don't think children like 
us are ready for it yet.

20:02.040 --> 20:05.910
Aw, just give it a try. 
What have you got to lose?

20:05.910 --> 20:09.550
I don't want to live with the memory that 
you tried to make us lose something.

20:10.040 --> 20:12.570
<i>That was a sharp comeback!</i>

20:12.980 --> 20:14.800
I'm sure they're delicious.

20:14.800 --> 20:18.060
You grew them with lots of love, after all.

20:20.370 --> 20:23.380
When you say they're full of love...

20:23.380 --> 20:25.580
...we have no choice but to eat them.

20:30.290 --> 20:32.950
Oh, yeah! I can eat this!

20:32.950 --> 20:35.340
They're veggies, but they taste so sweet!

20:35.340 --> 20:40.300
Perhaps I was mistaken about 
what vegetables truly were.

20:40.600 --> 20:44.800
Yay! My daughters got over 
their hatred of vegetables!

20:45.350 --> 20:46.970
Sorry for the wait!

20:46.970 --> 20:49.730
This is pound cake made 
with lots of carrots.

20:49.730 --> 20:51.810
Have it for dessert!

21:09.480 --> 21:11.480
Thanks, Sandra!

21:11.480 --> 21:13.770
You don't need to thank me.

21:13.770 --> 21:16.080
I'll be in your care from now on,

21:16.080 --> 21:18.240
so I need to be at least a bit useful...

21:20.920 --> 21:23.360
Come to think of it, there's one other rule

21:23.360 --> 21:26.160
for our house in the highlands 
that I forgot to tell you.

21:27.430 --> 21:31.540
It's to always remember to smile. Okay?

21:33.640 --> 21:36.440
I'm so glad to have you with us, Sandra!

21:36.710 --> 21:39.150
I'm glad to be here... Azusa.

23:09.910 --> 23:12.410
<b>Days in the Highlands</b>

23:10.250 --> 23:12.050
Days in the Highlands!

23:12.400 --> 23:14.930
You should tend to that 
garden every now and then.

23:14.930 --> 23:18.940
Not a problem. 
I've found new help, after all.

23:18.940 --> 23:19.800
Huh?

23:20.140 --> 23:22.980
Keep working until you can pay me back!

23:27.970 --> 23:29.170
Hangover?

23:29.570 --> 23:31.170
You leave me no choice.

23:30.180 --> 23:30.680
<b>Pluck!</b>

23:32.720 --> 23:34.780
I feel much better!

23:34.780 --> 23:36.330
You'd better be grateful.

23:36.330 --> 23:38.620
Now, time for another drink!

23:38.620 --> 23:39.750
Really?!
